          {
            "href": "#",
            "text": "Able-Bodied Adults Without Dependents Able-bodied adults between the ages of 18-54 (subject to change) without dependents (ABAWDs) are eligible for participation in SNAP for only three (3) months within a 36-month period of time without working or participating in a work or welfare program for at least 20 hours weekly, averaged monthly, unless exempt. After exhausting the initial three (3) allowable months, ABAWD individuals meeting certain criteria may qualify for three (3) additional months of participation in the 36-month period."
          },
          {
            "href": "#",
            "text": "eligible Having met the qualifications to receive a SNAP benefit by meeting the specified nonfinancial and financial requirements of eligibility."
          },
          {
            "href": "#",
            "text": "Waived Reservations 07/01/2025 through 10/31/2025"
          },
          {
            "href": "#",
            "text": "WAIVED COUNTIES 07/01/2025 through 10/31/2025"
          },
          {
            "href": "#",
            "text": "reservation The geographically defined area over which an Indian Tribal Organization (ITO) exercises governmental jurisdiction as long as the area is legally recognized by the Federal or State government as being set aside for the use of Indians."
          },
          {
